      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Direct fractional restoration (experimental)\n\nModels: `kandinsky_imagesr_2.0.safetensors` (huggingface.co/hmdlsk/Kandinsky-ImageSR-2.0-ComfyUI) in `ComfyUI/models/diffusion_models/` and the FLUX.1 VAE `ae.safetensors` in `ComfyUI/models/vae/`.\n\n**direct_fractional** restores directly at the output size: the model sees 1024-pixel tiles sampled from the input at the requested scale, so the number of model evaluations follows the output size (a 4576 px input at 1.2x needs 49 tiles instead of the 144 of a 2x restoration). The *native restoration scale* only selects which calibrated timesteps are reused (here the 2x family); the model was calibrated for 2x and 4x only, so this mode is **uncalibrated**. **correction_strength** scales the model's correction (z - strength * t * v) while the model stays conditioned on the creativity timestep.\n\nThis workflow restores directly at 1.2x with the 2x creativity-1 timestep and correction strength 0.5, a provisional value from a small CPU study (see the README). Use the calibrated mode (workflow 06) when maximum fidelity matters more than speed."
      ],
      "title": "Kandinsky ImageSR",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
